      "steps": [
        "Buy a ticket for an open Villager Rescue location and complete the roughly one-hour experience in person.",
        "Collect your cape code. Some cities email it after your visit. Others hand you a printed code card when you return your Orb of Interaction at the exit. Cities that use cards don't send emails.",
        "Redeem the code at <a href=\"https://www.minecraft.net/en-us/redeem\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">minecraft.net/redeem</a>. The cape unlocks on Java and Bedrock.",
        "Redeem within <b>30 days after the city you visited closes</b>. To be safe, redeem right away."
      ],
      "editionNotes": {
        "java": "On Java it's called the \"Minecraft Experience Cape\". Equip it in the Launcher or on your minecraft.net profile.",
        "bedrock": "On Bedrock it's called the \"Villager Rescue Cape\". Equip it from Dressing Room → Capes."
      },
      "notes": [
        "Venue dates are local to each city. Hours vary by day, so check the city page before you go."
